  "methodology": {
    "description": "Demand charges are a component of certain network tariffs that charge customers based on their peak electricity demand (measured in kW) during specified time windows. Unlike energy charges ($/kWh) which are based on total consumption, demand charges incentivise reducing peak usage — the single highest draw during the billing period determines the charge. This means running multiple high-power appliances simultaneously during peak hours costs more than spreading usage throughout the day.",
